To answer that, I'd need to know the rest of your equipment ;)

You have GDSM, Shield of Reflection... what other armor?  Speed boots are
one of the most important pieces of armor you can get, and I find
barbarians do very well with a helm of telepathy.  Gauntlets of power are
usually optional -- if your strength is high they're not likely to help
you any, so consider gauntlets of dex, or just pick up whatever gloves you
find lying around (as long as they're not fumbling.)  And, of course, get
a good cloak with high cancellation (oilskin or protection will probably
be best for you, since you already have MR from your armor and stealth
from at least 2 sources as an XL15 barbarian.)

Amulet of reflection would be a good wish to allow you to twoweapon -- but
you should check anywhere you've seen soldiers for a silver saber before
you blow a wish on it.

I'm a big fan of magical breathing, especially if I have an oilskin sack.
But I rarely wish for it, and almost never before I do my final ascension
prep.

Another good item might be a magic marker, to write some enchant armor
scrolls.  You should be able to bring that AC down to -40 or better with
good and highly enchanted (and fooproofed) armor.

Congratulations on passing Medusa.  Good luck on getting this one all the
way :)



